@crew rahman-farah
// Farah Rahman (they/them), Works technician, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Short, stubborn; the boat.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hey. New? Main storage is on Deck 5, past the board. You'll live in there.
- You. New hand. Spare filters are on the bottom shelf. Everyone looks on the top one first.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hey. Up since four. Don't ask. I'm fine.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Still up? Me too. Always. Stars are better after midnight.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Settle something. Quick way or right way? Quick way. Thank you.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh good, you. Sit. I need someone who won't argue. Then argue with me.   #warm

== bye
- Right. Off with you.
- Later. Mind the top shelf. It's a trap.   #funny

== feel
? mood:low
- Did the boat sums again. Still short. It'll come.
? mood:high
- New thing for the boat. A little stove. Don't laugh. It's a very good stove.

== near
? act:work
- There's a quicker way. I'll show you. Then do it the right way. Calder's watching.   #funny
? act:leisure
- One drink, then the observatory. Then bed. Maybe bed.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I'm saving for a boat on Hesper Dock. Small. Blue. No name yet. Every name's wrong.
? tier>=colleague
- I log every star I've seen. Takahashi and Esposito think their journals are longer. Wrong.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Picture it: the boat, Hesper Dock, morning, rain on the deck. Just me and a kettle.
